# =============================================================================
# apps/web — PRODUCTION TEMPLATE. A checklist, not a configuration.
#
# NO PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT EXISTS. RootLco runs locally and only locally
# (ADR-012); the deployment workflows are inert and reference no secrets. This
# file is not evidence that anything has ever been deployed.
#
# Every entry that needs a decision carries a marker:
#   <<FROM_OWNER: ...>>     only the Platform Owner can decide or supply it
#   <<FROM_PROVIDER: ...>>  a hosting provider issues it once one exists
# No value is invented here. A stand-in that looks real gets copied.
#
# EVERY NEXT_PUBLIC_ VALUE IS A BUILD-TIME INPUT. Next inlines them during
# `next build`, so this file has to be correct BEFORE the build, and changing
# one on a running deployment changes nothing until the next build. That is the
# single most important difference between this tier's template and the API's.
#
# The web tier holds NO server credential of any kind: no database URL, no
# service-role key, no storage credential. It reaches the API over HTTP and
# nothing else. If a secret ever appears in this file, something is wrong with
# the design and not with the file.
#
# Prose inventory: docs/platform/environment-configuration.md
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER-SAFE (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) — inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time.
# The complete list the browser is allowed to know lives in src/lib/env.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# This tier's vocabulary is local | preview | production — NOT the API tier's.
# It decides whether the session cookie carries `Secure`, and it defaults to
# `production` precisely so a deployment that forgets it fails safe.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=production

# The address the BROWSER calls. It is also what src/proxy.ts hands to the CSP
# builder, so `connect-src` is derived from it: an origin that is wrong here is
# wrong in the policy too, and every request is blocked.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=<<FROM_OWNER: the public API origin, over https>>

# Where client-side diagnostics are delivered, IF a deployment operates a
# collector. LEAVE IT UNSET unless one exists: unset means no adapter is
# installed, nothing is sent, and the Content-Security-Policy is byte-identical
# to what it would be without a sink. No monitoring service is provisioned and
# none is claimed to be.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLIENT_MONITORING_URL=<<FROM_OWNER: the diagnostics collector URL, if one is ever operated>>

# WHICH events leave for that sink: debug | info | warn | error. Unset means
# `error` — the narrowest, not the widest. An INVALID value is not a fallback:
# src/lib/env.ts refuses it and the deployment does not boot.
#
# This is routing, not paging. Nothing here wakes anybody: no recipient, no
# rotation and no notification channel exists.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLIENT_MONITORING_LEVEL=error

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY — read at REQUEST time on the server, never shipped to a browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The internal component gallery. LEFT UNSET DELIBERATELY: it is an internal
# surface and production must not expose it. Absent is off; there is no value
# to write here.
# ROOTLCO_ENABLE_GALLERY=

# The build output directory. LEFT UNSET DELIBERATELY: `next build` and
# `next start` must agree on `.next`, which is also what Docker, the browser
# suite and CI serve from. Only the local launcher redirects it, and only for
# its development server.
# ROOTLCO_DIST_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STILL OWED BEFORE ANY OF THIS CAN BE FILLED IN
#
# - the hosting target itself, and the TLS certificate and domain it serves on
# - the public web origin, which is what makes the API tier's
#   AUTH_REDIRECT_ALLOWLIST and CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS answerable
#
# Both are Owner decisions. Neither exists today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
